From: aiden build <build@aiden.local>
Subject: [PATCH] adb: add missing <functional> includes for libstdc++

Several adb headers use std::function<> without including <functional>.
Android's libc++ provides it transitively, but GCC 8.3's libstdc++ does
not, so the build fails with:

  tls_connection.h:51:31: error: 'function' in namespace 'std' does not
  name a template type
    using CertVerifyCb = std::function<int(X509_STORE_CTX*)>;

Add the missing include to the three headers that declare std::function
members/parameters: adb.h, services.h and tls/.../tls_connection.h.

Aiden-local patch (not from upstream nmeum/android-tools).
---
--- a/vendor/core/adb/adb.h
+++ b/vendor/core/adb/adb.h
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include <stdint.h>
 #include <sys/types.h>
 
+#include <functional>
 #include <string>
 
 #include <android-base/macros.h>
--- a/vendor/core/adb/services.h
+++ b/vendor/core/adb/services.h
@@ -17,6 +17,8 @@
 #ifndef SERVICES_H_
 #define SERVICES_H_
 
+#include <functional>
+
 #include "adb_unique_fd.h"
 
 constexpr char kShellServiceArgRaw[] = "raw";
--- a/vendor/core/adb/tls/include/adb/tls/tls_connection.h
+++ b/vendor/core/adb/tls/include/adb/tls/tls_connection.h
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include <stdint.h>
 
 #include <string_view>
+#include <functional>
 #include <vector>
 
 #include <android-base/unique_fd.h>
